[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-4718"] :question/problem "Find ${F}^{′}(0)$ if $F(x)={\\int }_{x}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}\\sqrt[3]{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, both the lower and upper limits contain a variable. However, to apply FTC II, we need the variable to be on the upper limit only. So, we can split the integral into two integrals, and rewrite them so that in both cases the variable is on the upper limit. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{x}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}\\sqrt[3]{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{x}^{a}\\sqrt[3]{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}\\sqrt[3]{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{a}^{x}\\sqrt[3]{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}\\sqrt[3]{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is any constant number between $x$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\nThe integrand $\\sqrt[3]{1+{t}^{2}}$ is continuous for all $t,$ so applying FTC II gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{\\int }_{a}^{x}\\sqrt[3]{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}\\sqrt[3]{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{a}^{x}\\sqrt[3]{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{a}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\sqrt[3]{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\sqrt[3]{1+{x}^{2}}+\\frac{\\text{du}}{\\text{d}x}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({\\int }_{a}^{u}\\sqrt[3]{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\sqrt[3]{1+{x}^{2}}+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))\\sqrt[3]{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\sqrt[3]{1+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))^{2}}-\\sqrt[3]{1+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\sqrt[3]{1+{sin}^{2}⁡(x)}-\\sqrt[3]{1+{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used the substitution $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\nFinally, we can compute ${F}^{′}(0).$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{′}(0) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)\\sqrt[3]{1+{sin}^{2}⁡(0)}-\\sqrt[3]{1+(0)^{2}} \\\\  & =1\\sqrt[3]{1}-\\sqrt[3]{1} \\\\  & =1-1 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-75221/selection/a56cba3f5959376a38c5c07f7934a7f40c8644762281ee8df98e7b4570c098fa" :answer/id #uuid "9cdebea1-63d9-550e-92b5-6e047eefe076" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{g}^{′}(2)=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75221/selection/431a5fca1045d2721512f21965a9b3d64a365d56f1f640bb029a8a0aace45181" :answer/id #uuid "cb0c9c36-1945-558d-a753-2ab62d123bf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{g}^{′}(2)=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75221/selection/e9e15735d8dc29d49f516a71f3cdba3f3a384f8ece30317c8f39577f5e123846" :answer/id #uuid "4255bb9d-f0a7-5348-a382-09a11c6d9490" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{g}^{′}(2)=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75221/selection/00d24677c2bf95c9f32a21537438d2670b51828523675276a54b3ea845fa0e04" :answer/id #uuid "42c6c102-1213-5b92-a66e-a68563ddf4f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{g}^{′}(2)=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75221/selection/4fcc6e0e4e224c18895ad6af51123c19c92cf0e2120c744e44be1f2fc12c1108" :answer/id #uuid "ff134327-c31d-5c37-89f5-2c0bce6c3642" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{g}^{′}(2)=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75221/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2e7ccd6d-95ff-5bdd-bd86-a85c5563fa5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-75221/selection/00d24677c2bf95c9f32a21537438d2670b51828523675276a54b3ea845fa0e04" :answer-field/choices ["q-75221/selection/a56cba3f5959376a38c5c07f7934a7f40c8644762281ee8df98e7b4570c098fa" "q-75221/selection/431a5fca1045d2721512f21965a9b3d64a365d56f1f640bb029a8a0aace45181" "q-75221/selection/e9e15735d8dc29d49f516a71f3cdba3f3a384f8ece30317c8f39577f5e123846" "q-75221/selection/00d24677c2bf95c9f32a21537438d2670b51828523675276a54b3ea845fa0e04" "q-75221/selection/4fcc6e0e4e224c18895ad6af51123c19c92cf0e2120c744e44be1f2fc12c1108"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75221" :question/id #uuid "71788e1c-b47b-5cdc-ab12-b5675e14b728" :question/math-academy-id "q-75221" :question/problem "Let $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)-x.$ Find ${g}^{′}(2)$ given the function is defined by $g(x)={\\int }_{x}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.$" :question/worked-solution "In this example, the variable limit $x$ is located on the lower limit. To apply FTC II, we need the variable to be on the upper limit. Using the properties of definite integrals, we can write\n\n$$\ng(x)={\\int }_{x}^{0}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)-t)\\,\\text{d}t=-{\\int }_{0}^{x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)-t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by FTC II, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}{\\int }_{x}^{0}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)-t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{\\int }_{0}^{x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)-t)\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{0}^{x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)-t)\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of ${g}^{′}(2),$ we substitute $x=2$ in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(2) & =-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 2)-2) \\\\  & =-(0-2) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-75221/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5075a64-0f91-58cf-b01b-5b71035f0680"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75221"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-116501/selection/282df39a15ba44d3d08b5c8cd23bc9330709bd3e3633154701d3195709c6af78" :answer/id #uuid "da048bd9-dc9a-50c0-af83-2b20072066fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116501/selection/fa78c15b6dc3a87ff5da29df199697731e92f5e09a5e33e59a9241d0dfc6c1a8" :answer/id #uuid "b31d9cec-e44d-5e1d-8ef2-481068b09d08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116501/selection/de0ddd6188b7aec25c0abd62ec585b488d0222130806797dadabfa6a97eed0d3" :answer/id #uuid "60e3e31e-30e9-54b5-9172-49580f7ed8cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116501/selection/f08d5d3568b9111bc347ec2c793c81d236c1041a29118211cddd31aa082793cf" :answer/id #uuid "feb24f6d-16b3-581e-804d-ef18536ea554" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116501/selection/983a5a3af3d85c03962a2091fbd40bc5b6ba5b2f87cbdae12aa67dc0ad0b730a" :answer/id #uuid "220cddc0-c466-5dbb-b6e3-43bc099f566f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116501/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9f8850dd-662c-5c77-822a-e1e3e6aa5880" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-116501/selection/fa78c15b6dc3a87ff5da29df199697731e92f5e09a5e33e59a9241d0dfc6c1a8" :answer-field/choices ["q-116501/selection/282df39a15ba44d3d08b5c8cd23bc9330709bd3e3633154701d3195709c6af78" "q-116501/selection/fa78c15b6dc3a87ff5da29df199697731e92f5e09a5e33e59a9241d0dfc6c1a8" "q-116501/selection/de0ddd6188b7aec25c0abd62ec585b488d0222130806797dadabfa6a97eed0d3" "q-116501/selection/f08d5d3568b9111bc347ec2c793c81d236c1041a29118211cddd31aa082793cf" "q-116501/selection/983a5a3af3d85c03962a2091fbd40bc5b6ba5b2f87cbdae12aa67dc0ad0b730a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-116501" :question/id #uuid "a3359bd2-48fb-59d6-ba98-93f115a49404" :question/math-academy-id "q-116501" :question/problem "For $x>0,$ find ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)={\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{t}\\,\\text{d}t.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute ${f}^{′}(x),$ we first make the substitution $u={x}^{2}$ and then we apply the chain rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}{\\int }_{0}^{u}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe integrand is continuous on $[0,u],$ and so by FTC II we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\cdot u\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{u} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})\\cdot u\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{u} \\\\  & =2x\\cdot {x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-116501/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0703e1b-2b81-5b95-b2ad-a7e42e702c21"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-116501"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-116504/selection/7502b379dc7945a795e13c4b2a01a9549f0fbafc98ef4d94991f89d9ec7646ea" :answer/id #uuid "ba1a8f2d-807f-543c-b853-55b7e69b3536" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-11)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116504/selection/1f07f73dea4be416ac592479b874a430fc5089c0a14fa258770c353e993e71d2" :answer/id #uuid "28c9f74a-2f55-5aa7-950e-aa47da69c492" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116504/selection/7c13d2beada7b01f0932c4935802cf65415aab8822d01b3483212f7422fce5e8" :answer/id #uuid "736bc42e-57b3-5f50-8aba-6d19a3773b84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x-11)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116504/selection/5e17883b7a02e41fa3e88d9a0c41f0904b8c41b503a711e6e7c6ffbdaafb9e13" :answer/id #uuid "4942eb32-f8ea-584f-8871-735413e1a855" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116504/selection/7a6f955519538448b3bc3da13e0e44735eeda0b21529400a16d2853497ade10a" :answer/id #uuid "5faf8e07-f4e3-5e39-abcf-3ccb6f01231e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x-11)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116504/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a6d8105d-5f9f-5b10-b6c1-79aa5aa0078e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-116504/selection/7a6f955519538448b3bc3da13e0e44735eeda0b21529400a16d2853497ade10a" :answer-field/choices ["q-116504/selection/7502b379dc7945a795e13c4b2a01a9549f0fbafc98ef4d94991f89d9ec7646ea" "q-116504/selection/1f07f73dea4be416ac592479b874a430fc5089c0a14fa258770c353e993e71d2" "q-116504/selection/7c13d2beada7b01f0932c4935802cf65415aab8822d01b3483212f7422fce5e8" "q-116504/selection/5e17883b7a02e41fa3e88d9a0c41f0904b8c41b503a711e6e7c6ffbdaafb9e13" "q-116504/selection/7a6f955519538448b3bc3da13e0e44735eeda0b21529400a16d2853497ade10a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-116504" :question/id #uuid "f496b800-2ee8-5e43-a695-4b3e8a838990" :question/math-academy-id "q-116504" :question/problem "Determine ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)={\\int }_{3x-5}^{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1)\\,\\text{d}t.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute ${f}^{′}(x),$ we first make the substitution $u=3x-5$ and then we apply the chain rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}{\\int }_{3x-5}^{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}{\\int }_{u}^{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe limit $u$ is located on the lower limit. To apply FTC II, we need the variable to be on the upper limit. Using the properties of the definite integrals, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}{\\int }_{u}^{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(-{\\int }_{1}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1)\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}{\\int }_{1}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by FTC II, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\cdot (-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}{\\int }_{1}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-1)\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2u-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3x-5)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2u-1)) \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(3x-5)-1) \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x-11).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-116504/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0703e1b-2b81-5b95-b2ad-a7e42e702c21"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-116504"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-116548/selection/3d456ef1cbfdc7a14d6d156150cea194f09eda5c0e034bea4252f6098b6187c9" :answer/id #uuid "b4d687a7-5b56-51cc-a2e5-1e5dd3769983" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116548/selection/8b8e8312d3c65ad7cceca7c10454819a39ba830369813e31c3feba32b8b084cf" :answer/id #uuid "67fa7e2e-b529-5b31-b2c0-733c60bd4f3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116548/selection/479877a90efcd7335f986cd026b9af50ab2755df1ea0ac3049ebbaf3ce5775db" :answer/id #uuid "f0a7aaef-775e-5c38-a90c-3b27c798a832" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116548/selection/c9794252b2bacf8ecc3ea1bfe1252d6670ffde6f394dbdae5bb7d57d05de8ff0" :answer/id #uuid "30a894d7-4c60-578d-8a3c-b50a5ab08cbd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116548/selection/52478ceff7976e597f5be59a5f3530710c312ac02d7a5519489d787efaa33ff8" :answer/id #uuid "fa8daae6-c46c-59c0-b4bc-632d83530bd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116548/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "24240ad9-c85e-50b8-9a3d-62011c712b64" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-116548/selection/8b8e8312d3c65ad7cceca7c10454819a39ba830369813e31c3feba32b8b084cf" :answer-field/choices ["q-116548/selection/3d456ef1cbfdc7a14d6d156150cea194f09eda5c0e034bea4252f6098b6187c9" "q-116548/selection/8b8e8312d3c65ad7cceca7c10454819a39ba830369813e31c3feba32b8b084cf" "q-116548/selection/479877a90efcd7335f986cd026b9af50ab2755df1ea0ac3049ebbaf3ce5775db" "q-116548/selection/c9794252b2bacf8ecc3ea1bfe1252d6670ffde6f394dbdae5bb7d57d05de8ff0" "q-116548/selection/52478ceff7976e597f5be59a5f3530710c312ac02d7a5519489d787efaa33ff8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-116548" :question/id #uuid "70a0aba7-0b5b-5702-ba2e-1ffda4c05a18" :question/math-academy-id "q-116548" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(0)$ if $f(x)={\\int }_{x}^{{3}^{x}+2}(6t-7)\\,\\text{d}t.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, both the lower and upper limits contain a variable. However, to apply FTC II, we need the variable to be on the upper limit only. So, we can split the integral into two integrals, and rewrite them so that in both cases the variable is on the upper limit. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{x}^{{3}^{x}+2}(6t-7)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{x}^{a}(6t-7)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{{3}^{x}+2}(6t-7)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{a}^{x}(6t-7)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{{3}^{x}+2}(6t-7)\\,\\text{d}t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is any constant number between $x$ and ${3}^{x}+2.$\n\nThe integrand $(6t-7)$ is continuous for all $t,$ so applying the FTC II gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{\\int }_{a}^{x}(6t-7)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{{3}^{x}+2}(6t-7)\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{a}^{x}(6t-7)\\,\\text{d}t)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{a}^{{3}^{x}+2}(6t-7)\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-(6x-7)+\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({\\int }_{a}^{u}(6t-7)\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =7-6x+({3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3))(6u-7) \\\\  & =7-6x+({3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3))(6({3}^{x}+2)-7) \\\\  & =7-6x+({3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3))(6\\cdot {3}^{x}+5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used the substitution $u={3}^{x}+2.$\n\nFinally, we can compute ${f}^{′}(0).$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(0) & =7-6(0)+({3}^{0}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3))(6\\cdot {3}^{0}+5) \\\\  & =7+11\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-116548/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a0f285ec-4f37-5d0d-a65c-be3ca48c740f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-116548"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
